# Rust build artifacts
/target
# Every crate under `services/` is outside the workspace (see the root
# Cargo.toml), so each builds into its own target directory. Globbed on the
# member rather than named one by one: a second service must not have to
# remember to come back here.
/services/*/target
# OpenTofu downloads provider binaries here (hundreds of MB). The rule lives
# with the directory that can contain them rather than with the OpenTofu
# module itself: during stacked work the untracked directory travels across
# branch checkouts, so an ignore added higher up leaves the branches below it
# one `git add <dir>` away from committing a provider binary.
/services/*/tofu/.terraform/

# OpenTofu. What must never be committed is anything holding an operator's
# Slack signing secret: the variables file and the state file both do.
#
# The pattern is `*.tfvars`, not the exact name `terraform.tfvars`, because
# `prod.auto.tfvars` and `secrets.tfvars` are perfectly ordinary names — and
# what is being protected is the content, not one filename. The `.example` is
# committed and contains no real values.
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds provider
# versions and checksums, no secrets, and committing it is what makes a
# `tofu init` here resolve what CI validated — the same reason `Cargo.lock` is
# committed.
**/*.rs.bk

# Coverage
lcov.info
*.profraw

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local environment variables (never commit)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
